-- Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) -- s.27A-27C and remaining
-- Division 2 standard terms (s.38-43, 45, 48-50). Based on content
-- from the Western Australian Legislation website at 2026-09-07,
-- "Residential Tenancies Act 1987", State of Western Australia, CC BY 4.0.

§ `Part IV - Residential tenancy agreements`

§§ `Division 1A - Form of residential tenancy agreement and associated documents`

DECLARE `form actor` IS ONE OF
    `the lessor or property manager`
    `the tenant`

DECLARE `form action` IS ONE OF
    `ensure a written residential tenancy agreement is in the approved form`
    `give a copy of the prescribed information to each tenant`
    `prepare a property condition report and provide 2 copies to the tenant`
    `mark a copy of the property condition report and give it back`
    `conduct an inspection, prepare a final report and provide a copy to the tenant`

GIVEN `the lessor has entered into a written residential tenancy agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if the lessor has entered into a written residential tenancy agreement.
GIVETH A DEONTIC `form actor` `form action`
DECIDE `the written agreement must be in the approved form` IS
    IF `the lessor has entered into a written residential tenancy agreement`
    THEN
        PARTY `the lessor or property manager`
        MUST `ensure a written residential tenancy agreement is in the approved form`
        WITHIN 1
        HENCE FULFILLED
        LEST BREACH BY `the lessor or property manager` BECAUSE "written residential tenancy agreement was not in the approved form (s.27A)"
    ELSE FULFILLED

GIVEN `the agreement is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if the residential tenancy agreement is in writing; FALSE if not.
GIVETH A DEONTIC `form actor` `form action`
DECIDE `the prescribed information must be given to each tenant` IS
    IF `the agreement is in writing`
    THEN
        PARTY `the lessor or property manager`
        MUST `give a copy of the prescribed information to each tenant`
        WITHIN 0
        HENCE FULFILLED
        LEST BREACH BY `the lessor or property manager` BECAUSE "prescribed information was not given to each tenant at the time of entering into the written agreement (s.27B(a))"
    ELSE
        PARTY `the lessor or property manager`
        MUST `give a copy of the prescribed information to each tenant`
        WITHIN 14
        HENCE FULFILLED
        LEST BREACH BY `the lessor or property manager` BECAUSE "prescribed information was not given to each tenant within 14 days after the tenant took possession (s.27B(b))"

GIVETH A DEONTIC `form actor` `form action`
`the start of tenancy property condition report must be given` MEANS
    PARTY `the lessor or property manager`
    MUST `prepare a property condition report and provide 2 copies to the tenant`
    WITHIN 7
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the lessor or property manager` BECAUSE "property condition report was not prepared and 2 copies provided within 7 days after the tenant entered into occupation (s.27C(1))"

GIVETH A DEONTIC `form actor` `form action`
`the final property condition report must be given` MEANS
    PARTY `the lessor or property manager`
    MUST `conduct an inspection, prepare a final report and provide a copy to the tenant`
    WITHIN 14
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the lessor or property manager` BECAUSE "final property condition report was not provided within 14 days after termination (s.27C(4))"

DECLARE `start of tenancy report` HAS
    `the tenant was given copies of the report` IS A BOOLEAN
    `days after the tenant received the copies` IS A NUMBER
    `the tenant has given a marked copy back to the lessor or property manager` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s.27C(3)
@export Decide whether the tenant is taken to accept the start-of-tenancy property condition report
GIVEN r IS A `start of tenancy report` @desc Whether the tenant was given copies of the s.27C(1) report, how many days have passed, and whether the tenant gave a marked copy back. If the tenant does not give a copy back within 7 days of receiving the copies, the tenant is taken to accept the report.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the tenant is taken to accept the report as a true and accurate description of the condition of the premises` IF
        r's `the tenant was given copies of the report`
    AND NOT r's `the tenant has given a marked copy back to the lessor or property manager`
    AND r's `days after the tenant received the copies` GREATER THAN 7

§§ `Division 2 - General standard terms`

DECLARE `premises condition` HAS
    `the tenant has kept the premises in a reasonable state of cleanliness` IS A BOOLEAN
    `there is damage to the premises` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the tenant has notified the lessor as soon as practicable after the damage` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the tenant has intentionally or negligently caused or permitted damage to the premises or a common area or chattels in the common area` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the tenant has used the premises, or caused or permitted the premises to be used, for any illegal purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the tenant has caused or permitted a nuisance` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the tenant had vacant possession of the premises on the day the tenant was entitled to enter into occupation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `there is a legal impediment to occupation of the premises as a residence of which at the time of entering into the agreement the lessor had or ought reasonably to have had knowledge` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the lessor delivered up vacant possession in a reasonable state of cleanliness and a reasonable state of repair having regard to age and character` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the lessor has maintained the premises in a reasonable state of repair having regard to age and character` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the lessor has conducted any repairs within a reasonable period after the need for the repair arose` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the lessor has complied with all requirements in respect of buildings, health and safety under any other written law insofar as they apply to the premises` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s.38
@export Decide whether the tenant is in breach of the cleanliness and damage term in s.38
GIVEN p IS A `premises condition` @desc Whether the tenant has kept the premises (including chattels provided with them) reasonably clean, notified damage as soon as practicable, and not intentionally or negligently caused or permitted damage to the premises or a common area.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the tenant is in breach of the cleanliness and damage term` IF
        NOT p's `the tenant has kept the premises in a reasonable state of cleanliness`
    OR  (
            p's `there is damage to the premises`
        AND NOT p's `the tenant has notified the lessor as soon as practicable after the damage`
        )
    OR  p's `the tenant has intentionally or negligently caused or permitted damage to the premises or a common area or chattels in the common area`

@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s.39
@export Decide whether the tenant is in breach of the conduct term in s.39
GIVEN p IS A `premises condition` @desc Whether the tenant has used the premises for an illegal purpose or caused or permitted a nuisance.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the tenant is in breach of the conduct term` IF
        p's `the tenant has used the premises, or caused or permitted the premises to be used, for any illegal purpose`
    OR  p's `the tenant has caused or permitted a nuisance`

@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s.40
@export Decide whether the tenant had vacant possession as required by s.40
GIVEN p IS A `premises condition` @desc Whether the tenant had vacant possession of the premises (excluding parts without exclusive occupation or agreed no-access parts) on the day the tenant was entitled to enter into occupation.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the tenant had vacant possession as required` IF
    p's `the tenant had vacant possession of the premises on the day the tenant was entitled to enter into occupation`

@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s.41
@export Decide whether the lessor is in breach of the legal-impediment term in s.41
GIVEN p IS A `premises condition` @desc Whether, at the time of entering into the agreement, there was a legal impediment to occupation as a residence of which the lessor had or ought reasonably to have had knowledge.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the lessor is in breach of the legal impediment term` IF
    p's `there is a legal impediment to occupation of the premises as a residence of which at the time of entering into the agreement the lessor had or ought reasonably to have had knowledge`

@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s.42
@export Decide whether the lessor is in breach of the cleanliness and repairs term in s.42
GIVEN p IS A `premises condition` @desc Whether the lessor delivered up vacant possession in a reasonable state of cleanliness and repair having regard to age and character, has maintained the premises, has conducted repairs within a reasonable period, and has complied with building, health and safety written laws.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the lessor is in breach of the cleanliness and repairs term` IF
        NOT p's `the lessor delivered up vacant possession in a reasonable state of cleanliness and a reasonable state of repair having regard to age and character`
    OR  NOT p's `the lessor has maintained the premises in a reasonable state of repair having regard to age and character`
    OR  NOT p's `the lessor has conducted any repairs within a reasonable period after the need for the repair arose`
    OR  NOT p's `the lessor has complied with all requirements in respect of buildings, health and safety under any other written law insofar as they apply to the premises`

DECLARE `urgent repair` HAS
    `the need for urgent repairs arose otherwise than as a result of a breach of the agreement by the tenant` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the tenant has notified the lessor of the need as soon as practicable after the need arose` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the lessor has ensured that the repairs are carried out by a suitable repairer as soon as practicable after that notification` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the repairs are necessary for the supply or restoration of a prescribed essential service` IS A BOOLEAN
    `hours after the need for the urgent repairs arose` IS A NUMBER
    `the tenant was unable to contact the lessor or the lessor failed to ensure the repairs were carried out by a suitable repairer as soon as practicable after notification` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the tenant has arranged for a suitable repairer to carry out the repairs to the minimum extent necessary` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN r IS A `urgent repair`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the prescribed period for urgent repairs has elapsed` IF
    IF r's `the repairs are necessary for the supply or restoration of a prescribed essential service`
    THEN r's `hours after the need for the urgent repairs arose` AT LEAST 24
    ELSE r's `hours after the need for the urgent repairs arose` AT LEAST 48

@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s.43
@export Decide whether the tenant may arrange urgent repairs under s.43(3)
GIVEN r IS A `urgent repair` @desc Urgent repairs needed otherwise than from the tenant's breach. Essential-service repairs: 24 hours. Other urgent repairs: 48 hours. The tenant may arrange a suitable repairer to the minimum extent necessary if, within that period, the tenant cannot contact the lessor or the lessor fails to ensure the repairs are carried out as soon as practicable after notification.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the tenant may arrange urgent repairs` IF
        r's `the need for urgent repairs arose otherwise than as a result of a breach of the agreement by the tenant`
    AND `the prescribed period for urgent repairs has elapsed` r
    AND r's `the tenant was unable to contact the lessor or the lessor failed to ensure the repairs were carried out by a suitable repairer as soon as practicable after notification`

DECLARE `lock change` HAS
    `the tenant's interest has been terminated under section 60(1)(bc)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is necessary to prevent the commission of family violence that the tenant suspects on reasonable grounds is likely to be committed against the tenant or a dependant of the tenant` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the lessor is a person reasonably suspected of being likely to commit that family violence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `days after the lock or other means of securing the premises has been altered or added` IS A NUMBER
    `the tenant has given the lessor a copy of the key` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s.45(2)
@export Decide whether the tenant may alter or add a lock without the lessor's consent under s.45(2)(a)
GIVEN l IS A `lock change` @desc After termination of a person's interest under s.60(1)(bc), or if necessary to prevent family violence the tenant suspects on reasonable grounds is likely.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the tenant may alter or add a lock without the lessor's consent` IF
        l's `the tenant's interest has been terminated under section 60(1)(bc)`
    OR  l's `it is necessary to prevent the commission of family violence that the tenant suspects on reasonable grounds is likely to be committed against the tenant or a dependant of the tenant`

GIVEN l IS A `lock change`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the tenant must give the lessor a copy of the key` IF
        `the tenant may alter or add a lock without the lessor's consent` l
    AND NOT l's `the lessor is a person reasonably suspected of being likely to commit that family violence`

DECLARE `assignment` HAS
    `the agreement provides that the tenant may assign or sublet` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the agreement provides that the tenant shall not assign or sublet` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the agreement provides that the tenant may assign or sublet only with the written consent of the lessor` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the lessor has unreasonably withheld consent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the lessor has charged more than the lessor's reasonable expenses incidental to giving consent` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN a IS A `assignment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the agreement is deemed to require the lessor's written consent to assign or sublet` IF
        NOT a's `the agreement provides that the tenant may assign or sublet`
    AND NOT a's `the agreement provides that the tenant shall not assign or sublet`
    AND NOT a's `the agreement provides that the tenant may assign or sublet only with the written consent of the lessor`

@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s.49
@export Decide whether the lessor is in breach of the assignment or subletting consent term in s.49(2)
GIVEN a IS A `assignment` @desc Applies where the agreement makes or is deemed to make the provision that the tenant may assign or sublet only with written consent. The lessor shall not unreasonably withhold consent or charge more than reasonable incidental expenses.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the lessor is in breach of the assignment or subletting consent term` IF
        (
            a's `the agreement provides that the tenant may assign or sublet only with the written consent of the lessor`
        OR  `the agreement is deemed to require the lessor's written consent to assign or sublet` a
        )
    AND (
            a's `the lessor has unreasonably withheld consent`
        OR  a's `the lessor has charged more than the lessor's reasonable expenses incidental to giving consent`
        )

DECLARE `vicarious facts` HAS
    `a person other than the tenant is lawfully on the premises` IS A BOOLEAN
    `that person's authority to be on the premises derives from the permission, express or implied, of the tenant` IS A BOOLEAN
    `that person did an act or omission that would if done by the tenant have constituted a breach of the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s.50
@export Decide whether the tenant is vicariously responsible under s.50
GIVEN v IS A `vicarious facts` @desc A person other than the tenant lawfully on the premises whose authority derives from the tenant's permission. The tenant is vicariously responsible for that person's act or omission that would have been a breach if done by the tenant.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the tenant is vicariously responsible` IF
        v's `a person other than the tenant is lawfully on the premises`
    AND v's `that person's authority to be on the premises derives from the permission, express or implied, of the tenant`
    AND v's `that person did an act or omission that would if done by the tenant have constituted a breach of the agreement`

§§§ `48. Lessor to bear outgoings in respect of premises`

DECLARE `outgoing` HAS
    `the amount is a rate, tax or charge imposed in respect of the premises under the Local Government Act 1995` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the amount is a rate, tax or charge imposed in respect of the premises under the Land Tax Act 2002` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the amount is a rate, tax or charge imposed for water supply or sewerage services under the Water Agencies (Powers) Act 1984 other than a charge for water consumed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the amount is a contribution payable to a community corporation under the Community Titles Act 2018 or a strata company under the Strata Titles Act 1985` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s.48
@export Decide whether the lessor shall bear an outgoing under s.48
GIVEN o IS A `outgoing` @desc The lessor shall bear rates, taxes or charges under the Local Government Act 1995, the Land Tax Act 2002, or water-supply or sewerage charges under the Water Agencies (Powers) Act 1984 other than a charge for water consumed. Contributions to a community corporation or strata company cannot be passed on to a tenant.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the lessor shall bear the outgoing` IF
        o's `the amount is a rate, tax or charge imposed in respect of the premises under the Local Government Act 1995`
    OR  o's `the amount is a rate, tax or charge imposed in respect of the premises under the Land Tax Act 2002`
    OR  o's `the amount is a rate, tax or charge imposed for water supply or sewerage services under the Water Agencies (Powers) Act 1984 other than a charge for water consumed`
    OR  o's `the amount is a contribution payable to a community corporation under the Community Titles Act 2018 or a strata company under the Strata Titles Act 1985`

§§§ `49A. Lessor's and tenant's responsibilities in respect of public utility services`

DECLARE `utility charge` HAS
    `a public utility service is provided in relation to the premises under a contract between the provider and the lessor or a strata company` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the charge is for the tenant's consumption of the utility at the premises` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the tenant's consumption of the utility is separately metered` IS A BOOLEAN
    `consumption at the premises is not separately metered but the charge is calculated in accordance with a method previously agreed to in writing by the lessor and the tenant` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the lessor has given the tenant a written notice under section 49A(4) within 30 days after the lessor receives an invoice` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the tenancy ended within 30 days after the lessor received the invoice or the lessor received the invoice after the tenancy ended` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s.49A
@export Decide whether the tenant must pay a public-utility charge under s.49A(3)
GIVEN u IS A `utility charge` @desc The tenant must pay only if the charge is for the tenant's consumption, the consumption is separately metered or calculated by a method agreed in writing, and the lessor has given the s.49A(4) written notice within 30 days of the invoice, unless the tenancy ended within that 30 days or the invoice arrived after the tenancy ended.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the tenant must pay the charge for the public utility service` IF
        u's `a public utility service is provided in relation to the premises under a contract between the provider and the lessor or a strata company`
    AND u's `the charge is for the tenant's consumption of the utility at the premises`
    AND (
            u's `the tenant's consumption of the utility is separately metered`
        OR  u's `consumption at the premises is not separately metered but the charge is calculated in accordance with a method previously agreed to in writing by the lessor and the tenant`
        )
    AND (
            u's `the lessor has given the tenant a written notice under section 49A(4) within 30 days after the lessor receives an invoice`
        OR  u's `the tenancy ended within 30 days after the lessor received the invoice or the lessor received the invoice after the tenancy ended`
        )

§§ `Fixtures`

`dirty premises not notified` MEANS `premises condition` WITH
    `the tenant has kept the premises in a reasonable state of cleanliness` IS FALSE,
    `there is damage to the premises` IS FALSE,
    `the tenant has notified the lessor as soon as practicable after the damage` IS TRUE,
    `the tenant has intentionally or negligently caused or permitted damage to the premises or a common area or chattels in the common area` IS FALSE,
    `the tenant has used the premises, or caused or permitted the premises to be used, for any illegal purpose` IS FALSE,
    `the tenant has caused or permitted a nuisance` IS FALSE,
    `the tenant had vacant possession of the premises on the day the tenant was entitled to enter into occupation` IS TRUE,
    `there is a legal impediment to occupation of the premises as a residence of which at the time of entering into the agreement the lessor had or ought reasonably to have had knowledge` IS FALSE,
    `the lessor delivered up vacant possession in a reasonable state of cleanliness and a reasonable state of repair having regard to age and character` IS TRUE,
    `the lessor has maintained the premises in a reasonable state of repair having regard to age and character` IS TRUE,
    `the lessor has conducted any repairs within a reasonable period after the need for the repair arose` IS TRUE,
    `the lessor has complied with all requirements in respect of buildings, health and safety under any other written law insofar as they apply to the premises` IS TRUE

`essential service 24 hours no contact` MEANS `urgent repair` WITH
    `the need for urgent repairs arose otherwise than as a result of a breach of the agreement by the tenant` IS TRUE,
    `the tenant has notified the lessor of the need as soon as practicable after the need arose` IS FALSE,
    `the lessor has ensured that the repairs are carried out by a suitable repairer as soon as practicable after that notification` IS FALSE,
    `the repairs are necessary for the supply or restoration of a prescribed essential service` IS TRUE,
    `hours after the need for the urgent repairs arose` IS 24,
    `the tenant was unable to contact the lessor or the lessor failed to ensure the repairs were carried out by a suitable repairer as soon as practicable after notification` IS TRUE,
    `the tenant has arranged for a suitable repairer to carry out the repairs to the minimum extent necessary` IS TRUE

`silent agreement on assignment` MEANS `assignment` WITH
    `the agreement provides that the tenant may assign or sublet` IS FALSE,
    `the agreement provides that the tenant shall not assign or sublet` IS FALSE,
    `the agreement provides that the tenant may assign or sublet only with the written consent of the lessor` IS FALSE,
    `the lessor has unreasonably withheld consent` IS TRUE,
    `the lessor has charged more than the lessor's reasonable expenses incidental to giving consent` IS FALSE

`guest caused a breach` MEANS `vicarious facts` WITH
    `a person other than the tenant is lawfully on the premises` IS TRUE,
    `that person's authority to be on the premises derives from the permission, express or implied, of the tenant` IS TRUE,
    `that person did an act or omission that would if done by the tenant have constituted a breach of the agreement` IS TRUE

`report not returned after 8 days` MEANS `start of tenancy report` WITH
    `the tenant was given copies of the report` IS TRUE,
    `days after the tenant received the copies` IS 8,
    `the tenant has given a marked copy back to the lessor or property manager` IS FALSE

#EVAL `the tenant is in breach of the cleanliness and damage term` `dirty premises not notified`
#EVAL `the tenant may arrange urgent repairs` `essential service 24 hours no contact`
#EVAL `the agreement is deemed to require the lessor's written consent to assign or sublet` `silent agreement on assignment`
#EVAL `the lessor is in breach of the assignment or subletting consent term` `silent agreement on assignment`
#EVAL `the tenant is vicariously responsible` `guest caused a breach`
#EVAL `the tenant is taken to accept the report as a true and accurate description of the condition of the premises` `report not returned after 8 days`
#ASSERT `the tenant is in breach of the cleanliness and damage term` `dirty premises not notified` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the tenant may arrange urgent repairs` `essential service 24 hours no contact` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the lessor is in breach of the assignment or subletting consent term` `silent agreement on assignment` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the tenant is vicariously responsible` `guest caused a breach` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the tenant is taken to accept the report as a true and accurate description of the condition of the premises` `report not returned after 8 days` EQUALS TRUE

#TRACE `the written agreement must be in the approved form` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the lessor or property manager` DOES `ensure a written residential tenancy agreement is in the approved form` AT 0

#TRACE `the start of tenancy property condition report must be given` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the lessor or property manager` DOES `prepare a property condition report and provide 2 copies to the tenant` AT 8

`land tax` MEANS `outgoing` WITH
    `the amount is a rate, tax or charge imposed in respect of the premises under the Local Government Act 1995` IS FALSE,
    `the amount is a rate, tax or charge imposed in respect of the premises under the Land Tax Act 2002` IS TRUE,
    `the amount is a rate, tax or charge imposed for water supply or sewerage services under the Water Agencies (Powers) Act 1984 other than a charge for water consumed` IS FALSE,
    `the amount is a contribution payable to a community corporation under the Community Titles Act 2018 or a strata company under the Strata Titles Act 1985` IS FALSE

`metered water with notice` MEANS `utility charge` WITH
    `a public utility service is provided in relation to the premises under a contract between the provider and the lessor or a strata company` IS TRUE,
    `the charge is for the tenant's consumption of the utility at the premises` IS TRUE,
    `the tenant's consumption of the utility is separately metered` IS TRUE,
    `consumption at the premises is not separately metered but the charge is calculated in accordance with a method previously agreed to in writing by the lessor and the tenant` IS FALSE,
    `the lessor has given the tenant a written notice under section 49A(4) within 30 days after the lessor receives an invoice` IS TRUE,
    `the tenancy ended within 30 days after the lessor received the invoice or the lessor received the invoice after the tenancy ended` IS FALSE

#EVAL `the lessor shall bear the outgoing` `land tax`
#EVAL `the tenant must pay the charge for the public utility service` `metered water with notice`
#ASSERT `the lessor shall bear the outgoing` `land tax` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the tenant must pay the charge for the public utility service` `metered water with notice` EQUALS TRUE
